WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
Gaussian Graphical Models read conditional
independence from the precision matrix,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:11.070
the inverse covariance: a zero entry means two
variables are conditionally independent,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.368
so a sparse precision matrix recovers the network.

00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:19.382
The ideal l-zero penalty that counts edges is
combinatorial and intractable.

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:23.473
Sub-l-one pseudo-norms approximate it well but are
non-convex,

00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:28.025
so most methods retreat to the convex l-one norm,
which over-shrinks,

00:00:28.105 --> 00:00:30.928
especially when variables outnumber samples.
